Dynamic Locators
---------------------
By cssSelector
======================
Css is cascaded style sheet , language which is used to design and provide styles
to webelement

-CssSelector is Locator which will identify element based css property
-cssSelector can travel in one direction (Parent to child node) and that is 
a reson it is faster then xpath
-cssSelector does not support methods

Syntax:
--------------
1.tagname with id
---------------------
Syntax:
-----------
tagname#id

Example
---------------
<input type="text" id="input-email" class="form-control">

input#input-email
Or
#input-email
=================================

2.tagname with attribute
--------------------------
Syntax:
-------------
tagname[attribute='value']

Example
------------
<input type="password" name="password" placeholder="Password">

input[placeholder='Password']

========================================
3.tagname with className
-----------------------------
Syntax:
------------
tagname.className

Example:
------------
<input type="submit" value="Login" class="btn btn-primary">

input.btn.btn-primary

4.tagname with id,attribute and className
-------------------------------------
Syntax
-------------
tagname#id.className[attribute='value']

Example:
----------------
<input type="submit" value="Login" class="btn btn-primary">

input[type='submit'].btn.btn-primary
================================================================

Css with special symbol
----------------------------------
1.* means contains()
---------------------------
To match element value partially we use *

Syntax:
---------------
tagname[attribute*='partial value']

Example
------------
<input id="twotabsearchtextbox">


input[id*='searchtext']

==============================================

2.^ means Startswith('prefix')
------------------------------
Syntax:
-----------
tagname[atrribute^='prefix value']

Example
------------
<input id="twotabsearchtextbox">

input[id^='two']
==============================================

3.$ means endsWith
--------------------
Syntax:
tagname[attribute$='suffix value']

Example
------------
<input id="twotabsearchtextbox">

input[id$='box']

